          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "We are in a fresh workspace. We need to compute eta radiative correction at given kinematic point.\n Steps:\n 1. Check available channels (should include eta).\n 2. Validate the kinematic point for the eta channel with standard CLAS12 settings.\n 3. If valid, generate input file(s) for EXCLURAD.\n 4. Write outcome.json and input files.\n\n However, note: the user only asks for the radiative correction at a single point. We can generate input for one point.\n\n We must use the exclurad MCP server tools.\n\n Let's start by listing channels to confirm eta is available and get default settings.\n",
